00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:45.700
Yeah, 49 pages.

344
00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:47.620
That's craziness.

345
00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:52.240
And you know how we've talked about how they would sort of rebuild the episodes in editing?

346
00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:55.580
Well, Erin had this quote that I absolutely loved.

347
00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:59.780
He said that Greg liked to rebuild the ship at sea.

348
00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:00.800
Oh, yeah.

349
00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:02.160
Isn't that such a great phrase?

350
00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:03.080
I love that.

351
00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:03.900
I just love that.

352
00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:07.120
Yeah, they would get in the editor's room, man, and they would just carve it up.

353
00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:12.840
And I told him, I said, it's always interesting for me now that we have all these scripts, thank you, James,

354
00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:17.440
to see what makes it on the screen and what doesn't and how they move everything around.

355
00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:21.200
And I'm always so happy with the final product, you know?

356
00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.080
But it's a cool thing to see.

357
00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:27.060
But I thought that Greg likes to rebuild the ship at sea was like a great phrase.

358
00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.380
Well, I think those were really good fast facts.

