00:24:47.270 --> 00:24:51.370
And if you go to four minutes, 11 seconds, you can see me talking to Andy.

542
00:24:51.570 --> 00:24:54.310
And I'm so delighted that Phyllis is messing up.

543
00:24:54.490 --> 00:24:58.190
And then Michael walks in and kind of yells at her and says, make the party, make the party.

544
00:24:58.190 --> 00:25:01.110
And then he leaves and Phyllis starts pumping the balloon.

545
00:25:01.490 --> 00:25:05.830
Well, Steve improvised, walking back in and saying, pump it, pump it.

546
00:25:05.930 --> 00:25:06.390
He did?

547
00:25:06.670 --> 00:25:06.950
He did.

548
00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:07.910
That was all improv.

549
00:25:08.270 --> 00:25:09.650
We just started cracking up.

550
00:25:09.730 --> 00:25:12.490
I thought I could see you starting to break in the background of that.

551
00:25:12.490 --> 00:25:12.690
Yeah.

552
00:25:12.810 --> 00:25:14.290
And Phyllis is starting to break too.

553
00:25:14.810 --> 00:25:21.470
So now Jim is at his desk and Pam is trying to tell him this story.

554
00:25:21.770 --> 00:25:22.790
I loved this.

555
00:25:22.930 --> 00:25:23.870
It was so funny.

556
00:25:24.050 --> 00:25:27.810
When she's like, Sarah Kaya comes in and he goes, oh, wait, Sarah Kaya comes in.

557
00:25:27.810 --> 00:25:31.590
And she's like, no, Sarah Kaya comes in.

558
00:25:32.350 --> 00:25:37.510
And then at the very end of the scene, when Dwight's like, who's Sarah Kaya comes in?

559
00:25:37.770 --> 00:25:38.970
That was improvised.

560
00:25:39.250 --> 00:25:39.870
It was?

561
00:25:40.090 --> 00:25:40.850
Rain improvised that.

562
00:25:40.970 --> 00:25:41.790
That's not in the script.

563
00:25:42.150 --> 00:25:43.250
Oh, my gosh.

564
00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:48.030
I watched this and I feel like I have had these conversations.

565
00:25:48.250 --> 00:25:48.570
Yes.

566
00:25:48.730 --> 00:25:49.530
A hundred percent.

567
00:25:49.790 --> 00:25:53.290
And I love the line when she's like, why can't you just be in art school with me?

568
00:25:54.430 --> 00:25:56.590
Because she's trying so hard to tell him the story.

569
00:25:56.950 --> 00:26:01.430
And, you know, this is the beginning of this storyline with Jim and Pam, where we're going

570
00:26:01.430 --> 00:26:06.830
to show that this distance has gone on for a while and maybe they're not connecting as

571
00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:08.390
easily as they used to.

572
00:26:08.550 --> 00:26:10.570
You know, long distance relationships are hard.

573
00:26:10.710 --> 00:26:15.650
And particularly when the people involved in your new life, the other person doesn't know.

574
00:26:15.930 --> 00:26:17.250
And it's kind of hard to keep track.

575
00:26:17.250 --> 00:26:18.410
Oh, yes.

576
00:26:18.590 --> 00:26:21.290
I mean, we experience this all the time when we go on locations.

577
00:26:21.870 --> 00:26:25.810
Or I remember Lee went on location to shoot a movie and he was directing a film.

578
00:26:26.110 --> 00:26:31.410
And he's trying to tell me this hilarious story about some prop mishap that happened.

579
00:26:31.570 --> 00:26:33.890
And everyone was laughing about these prop glasses.

580
00:26:34.270 --> 00:26:36.850
And I'm just like, I don't know who any of these people are.

581
00:26:36.990 --> 00:26:42.510
And what's really hard about it is that I like to be able to imagine the people or where

582
00:26:42.510 --> 00:26:43.110
they are.

583
00:26:43.810 --> 00:26:46.510
And we've talked about this when we get to a new place.

584
00:26:46.510 --> 00:26:50.470
Send me a video of where you are so that when I'm talking to you, I know what your little

585
00:26:50.470 --> 00:26:53.090
apartment looks like or I know what your room looks like.

586
00:26:53.170 --> 00:26:54.410
Yeah, I have to have that.

587
00:26:54.610 --> 00:26:57.370
Otherwise, I'm a little unsettled because I can't picture where you are.

588
00:26:57.670 --> 00:26:57.990
Yes.

589
00:26:58.170 --> 00:27:02.290
So I feel like that's what Pam and Jim are up against right now.

590
00:27:02.570 --> 00:27:04.250
Yeah, he doesn't know her world.

591
00:27:04.250 --> 00:27:07.290
And it's some of that location situation kind of stuff.

592
00:27:07.750 --> 00:27:09.070
I love the next scene.

593
00:27:10.750 --> 00:27:12.010
I love it so much.

594
00:27:12.010 --> 00:27:18.630
Angela is preparing this poster board full of baby photos because they're going to play

595
00:27:18.630 --> 00:27:23.130
a game where you have to guess which baby photo belongs to which employee.

596
00:27:23.570 --> 00:27:28.270
And Andy comes in and he mistakes Phyllis's baby photo for Angela.

597
00:27:28.650 --> 00:27:29.130
Mm-hmm.

598
00:27:29.390 --> 00:27:31.690
Will you please tell me about shooting this scene, Angela?

599
00:27:32.250 --> 00:27:35.330
Well, one of the reasons I storm off is because I started to laugh.

600
00:27:35.550 --> 00:27:36.130
I could tell.

601
00:27:36.130 --> 00:27:40.310
That was me trying to get out of there before you saw me laughing on camera.

602
00:27:40.490 --> 00:27:41.550
So here's the thing.

603
00:27:41.770 --> 00:27:43.290
Greg directed this episode, right?

604
00:27:43.450 --> 00:27:47.290
And he said, you guys, can you bring in your actual baby photos?

605
00:27:47.610 --> 00:27:50.470
And he said, if you don't have a baby photo, it could be like when you're a toddler.

606
00:27:50.790 --> 00:27:52.950
Just can I get photos of you guys when you were little?

607
00:27:53.150 --> 00:27:54.450
And we did, right?

608
00:27:54.450 --> 00:27:56.410
Yes, we got a lot of fan mail about that.

609
00:27:56.410 --> 00:27:59.130
Were these actual photos of the cast?

610
00:27:59.550 --> 00:28:00.170
They were.

611
00:28:00.390 --> 00:28:00.590
Yeah.

612
00:28:06.270 --> 00:28:10.050
Everyone else is an actual baby photo from their childhood.

613
00:28:10.310 --> 00:28:11.290
Including Amy Ryan.

614
00:28:11.470 --> 00:28:11.990
She's up there.

615
00:28:12.190 --> 00:28:12.550
Yes.

616
00:28:13.190 --> 00:28:14.430
And so is Mindy.

617
00:28:14.550 --> 00:28:15.830
I mean, we're all on the board.

618
00:28:15.930 --> 00:28:16.070
Yeah.

619
00:28:16.290 --> 00:28:16.710
We're all on the board.

620
00:28:17.090 --> 00:28:18.230
Jenna, what did I bring in today?

621
00:28:18.310 --> 00:28:19.090
Do you want to share with them?

622
00:28:19.270 --> 00:28:21.710
You brought in your baby photo.

623
00:28:21.910 --> 00:28:26.730
The one that was on the board with your little hand up on your little chubby cheek.

624
00:28:26.910 --> 00:28:27.450
I know.

625
00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:28.550
I know.

626
00:28:28.750 --> 00:28:30.350
You guys, it's really me.

627
00:28:30.490 --> 00:28:31.790
I get asked this all the time.

628
00:28:31.930 --> 00:28:35.310
And my mom, I called my mom and I said, mom, we're doing the baby shower episode.

629
00:28:35.310 --> 00:28:36.710
And it's my baby photo.

630
00:28:36.870 --> 00:28:38.490
And I want to know everything about it.

631
00:28:38.570 --> 00:28:42.070
She said, oh, I have several more of that same day where we put you in different poses.

632
00:28:43.350 --> 00:28:45.030
Oh, so there's more.

633
00:28:45.250 --> 00:28:47.030
But here's what my mom said.

634
00:28:47.090 --> 00:28:52.150
She took me to JCPenney's at the Acadiana Shopping Mall in Lafayette, Louisiana.

635
00:28:52.570 --> 00:28:54.410
I was around six months old.

636
00:28:54.650 --> 00:28:57.670
And apparently, I was born with just a ton of hair.

637
00:28:57.830 --> 00:28:59.350
And it was sort of an auburn brown.

638
00:28:59.630 --> 00:29:01.830
She said I had so much hair.

639
00:29:02.130 --> 00:29:04.830
Just right out of the gate, I had tons of hair.

640
00:29:05.430 --> 00:29:08.150
And so she tried to style it for the photo.

641
00:29:08.370 --> 00:29:11.650
I was like, mom, you gave me like a mohawk with bangs.

642
00:29:12.290 --> 00:29:15.730
So yeah, she said she had tried to put a little ribbon at the top.

643
00:29:15.930 --> 00:29:17.050
That would have made more sense.

644
00:29:17.270 --> 00:29:17.490
Right.

645
00:29:17.650 --> 00:29:19.810
But I don't know, it fell out or something.

646
00:29:20.010 --> 00:29:23.270
And then they propped me up on my hand like that.

647
00:29:24.350 --> 00:29:28.570
It's so funny because I remember those photo studio photo shoots.

648
00:29:28.770 --> 00:29:30.630
That was a thing of my childhood as well.

649
00:29:30.630 --> 00:29:33.390
And they would have these carpeted blocks.

650
00:29:33.630 --> 00:29:33.910
Yes.

651
00:29:34.130 --> 00:29:37.070
And you would like be propped up on a little carpeted block.

652
00:29:37.310 --> 00:29:39.870
I'm propped up because I can't sit yet, really.

653
00:29:40.890 --> 00:29:42.370
Anyway, there you go.

654
00:29:42.510 --> 00:29:44.410
That's my actual baby photo, you guys.

655
00:29:44.670 --> 00:29:49.970
Well, since mine wasn't on the board, I tell you what, I'll post mine on the Office Ladies pod.

656
00:29:49.970 --> 00:29:51.670
So you can see me as a baby too.

657
00:29:51.810 --> 00:29:52.110
Yes.

658
00:29:52.210 --> 00:29:55.790
And I'll ask my mom if she can find any other photos from that particular photo shoot.

659
00:29:56.910 --> 00:30:10.270
As Michael is preparing for Jan's arrival, he needs to tell Holly that he's going to be kind of cold to her today because he needs to protect Jan's feelings.

660
00:30:10.470 --> 00:30:11.970
Jan's bloated feelings.

661
00:30:12.210 --> 00:30:12.390
Yeah.

662
00:30:12.550 --> 00:30:14.090
Because Jan is going to come in.

663
00:30:14.170 --> 00:30:16.650
She's going to be so unattractive.

664
00:30:16.850 --> 00:30:18.490
And Holly is very attractive.

665
00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:20.710
And yeah, he just wants to be sensitive.

666
00:30:20.710 --> 00:30:22.670
So he warns her.

667
00:30:23.010 --> 00:30:25.510
But then Jan arrives.

668
00:30:25.970 --> 00:30:27.350
She's not pregnant.

669
00:30:27.650 --> 00:30:29.090
She has a baby.

670
00:30:29.410 --> 00:30:30.730
And she looks amazing.

671
00:30:31.050 --> 00:30:31.530
Yeah.

672
00:30:31.850 --> 00:30:33.110
But she's had the baby.

